Added pnpm run slideshow:to-site in ark-admin. It pushes local miniflare slideshow → remote R2 → runs ark-site sync:slideshow. Verified end-to-end just now.

Everyday workflow
1. Edit in admin (http://localhost:5173)
Open the slide.
Change image / crop / filters / HTML layer as needed.
Click Save slide (this also bakes crop/filter into image files).
Keep Published on if it should show on the site.
2. Push local → site (from ark-admin)
cd /home/dan/Desktop/ark-admin
pnpm run slideshow:to-site
That does:

Read local Vite/miniflare R2
Upload to remote ark-admin-content + ark-admin-media
Run pnpm run sync:slideshow in ../ark-site
If ark-site lives elsewhere:

ARK_SITE_ROOT=/path/to/ark-site pnpm run slideshow:to-site
3. View on Astro (http://localhost:4321)
Hard-refresh the browser (Ctrl+Shift+R).

Other commands
Command	What it does
pnpm run slideshow:to-site
Local miniflare → remote → ark-site sync (usual)
pnpm run slideshow:push-remote
Local → remote only (no site sync)
pnpm run slideshow:to-site -- --dry-run
List what would upload, no writes
In ark-site: pnpm run sync:slideshow
Remote → site only
Remember
Admin pnpm run dev writes to local R2. Astro sync reads remote R2. Always run slideshow:to-site after saves you want to see on the static site.
Crop/filter changes need Save slide first so baked -m-* / -d-* files exist locally, then slideshow:to-site.